1
00:00:02,385 --> 00:00:09,417
[Dive Into You]

2
00:00:10,047 --> 00:00:14,214
[This is a fictional story. All characters
and events bear no relation to reality]

3
00:00:40,853 --> 00:00:44,331
<i>♪ On a cold, rainy day ♪</i>

4
00:00:45,509 --> 00:00:50,441
[We Buy, Sell & Repair]
<i>♪ Sit in an old-fashioned coffeehouse ♪</i>

5
00:00:51,787 --> 00:00:56,805
<i>♪ Over a glass of Doraji whiskey ♪</i>

6
00:00:56,805 --> 00:01:02,344
<i>♪ And listen to that rich saxophone ♪</i>

7
00:01:13,490 --> 00:01:15,201
See anything you like?

8
00:01:15,201 --> 00:01:16,608
Oh, yes.

9
00:01:16,608 --> 00:01:18,608
How much is this?

10
00:01:20,489 --> 00:01:21,808
How much have you got?

11
00:01:21,808 --> 00:01:23,721
One second.

12
00:01:28,286 --> 00:01:30,046
Let's see...

13
00:01:30,686 --> 00:01:33,164
Give me a thousand won. It's yours.

14
00:01:33,164 --> 00:01:35,408
A thousand won? Seriously?

15
00:01:35,408 --> 00:01:37,317
Are you sure?

16
00:01:37,317 --> 00:01:38,859
Yeah.

17
00:01:46,630 --> 00:01:48,033
Thank you.

18
00:01:48,033 --> 00:01:51,038
Have fun shooting with it.

19
00:01:51,038 --> 00:01:52,808
And take good care of it.

20
00:01:52,808 --> 00:01:55,653
I will. Thank you so much!

21
00:01:55,653 --> 00:02:00,883
<i>♪ At my age, after all these years ♪</i>

22
00:02:00,883 --> 00:02:05,217
<i>♪ What sweetness could heartbreak hold? ♪</i>

23
00:02:05,217 --> 00:02:10,513
<i>♪ Still, there's an empty space ♪</i>

24
00:02:10,513 --> 00:02:15,008
<i>♪ Somewhere in my heart ♪</i>

25
00:02:15,008 --> 00:02:19,193
<i>♪ For all that I've lost ♪</i>

26
00:02:19,193 --> 00:02:20,356
[Episode 1]

27
00:02:32,906 --> 00:02:34,536
[2010 Haesol City
Superintendent's Cup Judo Tournament]

28
00:02:42,826 --> 00:02:45,720
- You got this!
- Go, Yoon Ha Ru!

29
00:02:46,389 --> 00:02:47,966
You too, Woo Jae!

30
00:02:47,966 --> 00:02:50,369
But Ha Ru, you better win!

31
00:03:18,471 --> 00:03:19,740
Start!

32
00:03:19,740 --> 00:03:21,565
[Boys' High School Division]
[Yoon Ha Ru, Haesol High School]

33
00:03:21,565 --> 00:03:23,873
- Go for it!
- Go!

34
00:03:23,873 --> 00:03:26,188
- You got this!
- Go, go!

35
00:03:28,330 --> 00:03:31,336
- Yoon Ha Ru!
- Yoon Ha Ru!

36
00:03:31,336 --> 00:03:33,404
- Yoon Ha Ru!
- Yoon Ha Ru!

37
00:03:35,596 --> 00:03:39,414
The world's best are going head-to-head
in the men's under-73-kilogram division

38
00:03:39,414 --> 00:03:41,311
here at the Arcadia judo competition.

39
00:03:41,311 --> 00:03:43,507
We're at Arcadia Arena in Japan.

40
00:03:43,507 --> 00:03:45,250
Korea's Yoon Ha Ru.

41
00:03:45,250 --> 00:03:49,490
He's up against Kenji Sato,
who's dominated this weight class.

42
00:03:49,490 --> 00:03:51,954
Ha Ru is down by a half point,

43
00:03:51,954 --> 00:03:54,991
so he needs a full point
to turn this match around.

44
00:03:54,991 --> 00:03:58,376
Sato has a half-point lead,
but he keeps attacking.

45
00:03:58,376 --> 00:04:00,082
- That's right.
- Come on!

46
00:04:03,762 --> 00:04:05,932
Ha Ru keeps getting caught by his attacks.

47
00:04:05,932 --> 00:04:06,782
Go for the lead leg!

48
00:04:06,782 --> 00:04:10,037
Sato has a half-point lead,
but he keeps attacking.

49
00:04:10,037 --> 00:04:12,441
That's right. And Yoon Ha Ru...

50
00:04:12,441 --> 00:04:14,134
- Shoulder throw...
- He goes for a shoulder throw!

51
00:04:14,134 --> 00:04:15,982
- That was close.
- He avoids it. Good!

52
00:04:15,982 --> 00:04:18,273
- He goes in for a throw!
- Yeah, Yoon Ha Ru...

53
00:04:18,273 --> 00:04:20,228
- Nice.
- Oh, but now...

54
00:04:20,228 --> 00:04:21,404
Ha Ru's underneath!

55
00:04:21,404 --> 00:04:22,516
He can't let Sato pin him...

56
00:04:22,516 --> 00:04:24,453
<i>Pinning is called!</i>

57
00:04:24,453 --> 00:04:25,547
<i>He has to get out!</i>

58
00:04:25,547 --> 00:04:27,617
Time is running out!
Yoon Ha Ru! He has to escape!

59
00:04:27,617 --> 00:04:29,639
- Yoon Ha Ru!
- He has to get out!

60
00:04:29,639 --> 00:04:31,176
Sato keeps pressing.

61
00:04:31,176 --> 00:04:32,012
- Yoon Ha Ru!
- Bridge...

62
00:04:32,012 --> 00:04:34,511
He's out! He escaped!

63
00:04:35,735 --> 00:04:38,169
- That was dangerous.
- It was!

64
00:04:39,295 --> 00:04:41,206
Stop!

65
00:04:41,206 --> 00:04:44,020
Stop is called, and they're reset.

66
00:04:44,020 --> 00:04:46,411
Ha Ru needs to watch the clock.

67
00:04:46,411 --> 00:04:49,018
Yes, he's racing against time now.

68
00:04:49,018 --> 00:04:52,512
There's not much time left.
He has to keep attacking.

69
00:04:52,512 --> 00:04:53,791
Exactly.

70
00:04:53,791 --> 00:04:55,041
He needs a full point.

71
00:04:55,041 --> 00:04:58,015
He has to think fast, react fast, and go in.

72
00:04:58,015 --> 00:05:01,225
He needs a full point to come back.
There's still time.

73
00:05:01,225 --> 00:05:01,920
Start!

74
00:05:01,920 --> 00:05:04,028
You can do it, Yoon Ha Ru!

75
00:05:04,028 --> 00:05:07,641
He needs to stay aggressive.

76
00:05:07,641 --> 00:05:08,752
Nice combination!

77
00:05:08,752 --> 00:05:10,105
He's still got plenty in the tank.

78
00:05:10,105 --> 00:05:11,675
Go! Yoon Ha Ru!

79
00:05:11,675 --> 00:05:13,661
Go for the lead leg!

80
00:05:13,661 --> 00:05:14,812
Ha Ru attacks!

81
00:05:14,812 --> 00:05:16,777
- No, watch the counter!
- Yoon Ha Ru!

82
00:05:16,777 --> 00:05:19,210
Now, can he...

83
00:05:28,961 --> 00:05:30,691
- He's done it!
- Nice!

84
00:05:30,691 --> 00:05:32,732
Yoon Ha Ru! Can you believe it?

85
00:05:32,732 --> 00:05:35,402
- Stop!
- Stop!

86
00:05:35,402 --> 00:05:36,573
A shoulder throw!

87
00:05:36,573 --> 00:05:38,257
Incredible! Korea's Yoon Ha Ru!

88
00:05:38,257 --> 00:05:41,604
He takes down the world's best, Kenji Sato!

89
00:05:41,604 --> 00:05:43,850
He was in a very tough spot just then.

90
00:05:43,850 --> 00:05:47,583
He went for a large outer reap,
and Sato tried to counter,

91
00:05:47,583 --> 00:05:49,909
but Ha Ru pulled his leg free
and transitioned into a shoulder throw.

92
00:05:49,909 --> 00:05:52,187
- What incredible focus!
- That was nice.

93
00:05:52,187 --> 00:05:53,717
He is unbelievable.

94
00:05:53,717 --> 00:05:55,062
- Amazing.
- Absolutely.

95
00:05:55,062 --> 00:05:59,293
<i>Yoon Ha Ru defeats Kenji Sato
and takes gold for Korea!</i>

96
00:06:04,089 --> 00:06:08,899
See? Ha Ru takes after me.
That's why he's so good!

97
00:06:08,899 --> 00:06:11,175
What are you talking about? He takes after me!

98
00:06:11,175 --> 00:06:13,406
[Judo Idol Yoon Ha Ru Wins Gold]
No! He takes after me!

99
00:06:13,406 --> 00:06:14,916
Quiet!

100
00:06:14,916 --> 00:06:18,253
With five seconds left,
you pulled off a dramatic shoulder throw.

101
00:06:18,253 --> 00:06:22,643
Everyone said beating Kenji Sato
would be impossible.

102
00:06:22,643 --> 00:06:24,907
I never thought it was impossible.

103
00:06:24,907 --> 00:06:27,680
I just felt like I was going to win.

104
00:06:27,680 --> 00:06:30,140
Did you have some kind of special feeling?

105
00:06:30,140 --> 00:06:32,378
Not a feeling, exactly...

106
00:06:32,378 --> 00:06:38,382
More like a special kind of faith and love.

107
00:06:38,382 --> 00:06:39,755
Actually...

108
00:06:39,755 --> 00:06:41,701
I'll be honest with you.

109
00:06:41,701 --> 00:06:43,539
Yes?

110
00:06:43,539 --> 00:06:47,158
More than when I threw Kenji Sato on that mat,

111
00:06:47,158 --> 00:06:51,757
seeing my fans from up here on the podium...

112
00:06:51,757 --> 00:06:54,409
makes my heart race even faster.

113
00:06:54,409 --> 00:06:58,593
Now I see why they call you the idol of judo.

114
00:06:58,593 --> 00:07:03,060
Would you say a few words
to everyone in Korea and your fans?

115
00:07:03,060 --> 00:07:04,585
Of course.

116
00:07:06,008 --> 00:07:09,792
To everyone in Korea
who supported me through these tough times,

117
00:07:09,792 --> 00:07:13,930
<i>and to all my fans
who have always stood by me...</i>

118
00:07:13,930 --> 00:07:18,909
your love and support
put this gold medal around my neck.

119
00:07:18,909 --> 00:07:20,734
I love you all.

120
00:07:22,112 --> 00:07:28,449
Any words for actress Yoon Ha Na?
She must be thrilled for you.

121
00:07:29,888 --> 00:07:31,488
Yoon Ha Na?

122
00:07:35,300 --> 00:07:36,419
[A Hollow Craft, Stripped of Sincerity]

123
00:07:36,419 --> 00:07:40,803
"Yoon Ha Na once burned with life,
becoming each role.

124
00:07:40,803 --> 00:07:44,769
Now, where her own emotions have dried up,

125
00:07:45,899 --> 00:07:51,046
she fills the void with soulless imitation."

126
00:08:21,069 --> 00:08:24,376
Congratulations, Ms. Yoon.

127
00:08:25,588 --> 00:08:27,278
For what?

128
00:08:27,278 --> 00:08:28,679
Sorry?

129
00:08:28,679 --> 00:08:30,791
Oh, well...

130
00:08:32,649 --> 00:08:34,673
Sorry. My mind was somewhere else.

131
00:08:34,673 --> 00:08:36,845
What were you congratulating me for?

132
00:08:36,845 --> 00:08:40,649
Yoon Ha Ru just won the gold medal.

133
00:08:40,649 --> 00:08:43,686
Oh, really? Thank you.

134
00:08:43,686 --> 00:08:47,029
With both of you doing so well,
your parents must be thrilled.

135
00:08:47,029 --> 00:08:48,042
Not really.

136
00:08:48,042 --> 00:08:51,085
By tomorrow, Ha Ru's ego
will be through the roof,

137
00:08:51,085 --> 00:08:53,270
and he'll drive us all crazy.

138
00:08:53,270 --> 00:08:57,424
I already can't stand him.

139
00:08:57,424 --> 00:08:59,034
Have some rest.

140
00:09:03,202 --> 00:09:05,189
What's up?

141
00:09:05,189 --> 00:09:06,942
Did he win?

142
00:09:10,604 --> 00:09:13,086
I have nothing to say to her.

143
00:09:13,086 --> 00:09:14,763
She probably didn't even watch my match.

144
00:09:14,763 --> 00:09:17,903
She couldn't care less about me.
All she does is tell me to quit showing off.

145
00:09:17,903 --> 00:09:19,071
So, nothing.

146
00:09:19,071 --> 00:09:21,513
You two really don't hold back with each other.

147
00:09:21,513 --> 00:09:24,977
Any final words before we wrap up?

148
00:09:24,977 --> 00:09:26,977
Final words...

149
00:09:28,988 --> 00:09:32,067
Actually, there's someone I really love.

150
00:09:32,067 --> 00:09:34,640
<i>I'd like to say something to him.</i>

151
00:09:34,640 --> 00:09:38,289
<i>Someone you really love?</i>

152
00:09:38,289 --> 00:09:40,791
<i>Now you've got me curious.</i>

153
00:09:40,791 --> 00:09:44,859
<i>He's a friend who's way better
at judo than I am.</i>

154
00:09:45,713 --> 00:09:46,968
[Judo Idol Yoon Ha Ru Wins Gold]

155
00:09:46,968 --> 00:09:49,050
<i>Hey, Jung Woo Jae!</i>

156
00:09:49,050 --> 00:09:50,796
<i>You watching?</i>

157
00:09:52,492 --> 00:09:54,566
<i>I kept my promise.</i>

158
00:09:56,426 --> 00:09:59,471
You did well, Yoon Ha Ru.

159
00:10:07,951 --> 00:10:11,521
There'll be even more reporters
than usual because of Ha Ru.

160
00:10:11,521 --> 00:10:13,651
Be on your game.

161
00:10:13,651 --> 00:10:15,465
I'm already doing enough.

162
00:10:15,465 --> 00:10:18,028
I was cheering on my twin even from overseas.

163
00:10:18,028 --> 00:10:21,629
I may look worn out,
but I should at least look happy.

164
00:10:21,629 --> 00:10:23,986
I need that close-sibling image.

165
00:10:23,986 --> 00:10:27,239
You're not selling it.

166
00:10:27,239 --> 00:10:29,263
Look at your face.

167
00:10:29,263 --> 00:10:32,139
Does that look like a happy face?

168
00:10:35,397 --> 00:10:40,071
You can fool reporters,
but you can't fool the camera.

169
00:10:40,071 --> 00:10:42,273
Oh, come on.

170
00:10:42,273 --> 00:10:46,786
I'm just prepping for my next role.
She's got a tragic past.

171
00:10:46,786 --> 00:10:48,156
Look at my eyes.

172
00:10:48,156 --> 00:10:50,077
More soulful, right?

173
00:10:50,077 --> 00:10:51,570
Yoon Ha Na.

174
00:10:51,570 --> 00:10:53,027
Yeah, CEO Seo Ye Rang.

175
00:10:53,027 --> 00:10:54,477
- You...
- Okay, okay.

176
00:10:54,477 --> 00:10:55,994
Stop worrying.

177
00:10:55,994 --> 00:10:57,211
You know who I am, right?

178
00:10:57,211 --> 00:10:59,259
I'm Yoon Ha Na.

179
00:11:00,047 --> 00:11:01,900
You're impossible.

180
00:11:11,870 --> 00:11:13,448
What's taking her so long?

181
00:11:13,448 --> 00:11:15,441
Ha Na.

182
00:11:15,441 --> 00:11:16,965
I want to see her already!

183
00:11:16,965 --> 00:11:18,442
When is she coming out?

184
00:11:18,442 --> 00:11:20,142
She's taking forever.

185
00:11:20,142 --> 00:11:22,283
I want to see her.

186
00:11:24,135 --> 00:11:25,560
Ha Na!

187
00:11:25,560 --> 00:11:26,697
She's here.

188
00:11:26,697 --> 00:11:27,992
All teams, hold formation.

189
00:11:27,992 --> 00:11:29,646
Moving out.

190
00:11:30,527 --> 00:11:32,013
Take it slow.

191
00:11:32,013 --> 00:11:33,828
- This way, please.
- Ha Na!

192
00:11:35,986 --> 00:11:37,197
One moment!

193
00:11:37,197 --> 00:11:40,209
As his twin, did you have
a feeling he would win?

194
00:11:40,209 --> 00:11:42,168
Any words for Yoon Ha Ru?

195
00:11:42,168 --> 00:11:45,938
Not really. I just knew he'd do well.

196
00:11:45,938 --> 00:11:47,644
Congrats, Ha Ru.

197
00:11:48,944 --> 00:11:51,224
- Did you expect him to win?
- Ha Na!

198
00:11:51,224 --> 00:11:52,924
Step back, please!

199
00:11:59,483 --> 00:12:00,586
The teddy bear's eye...

200
00:12:00,586 --> 00:12:02,319
What is that?

201
00:12:02,319 --> 00:12:04,621
Are you okay?

202
00:12:04,621 --> 00:12:07,060
- Who sent this?
- Ha Na! Are you okay?

203
00:12:07,060 --> 00:12:09,820
<i>You can't even cry!</i>

204
00:12:11,972 --> 00:12:15,169
<i>You can't even cry!</i>

205
00:12:16,915 --> 00:12:20,028
<i>You can't even cry!</i>

206
00:12:23,422 --> 00:12:25,628
Ha Na.

207
00:12:25,628 --> 00:12:28,082
We're on camera right now.

208
00:12:40,416 --> 00:12:41,874
Excuse me.

209
00:12:41,874 --> 00:12:43,150
Excuse me.

210
00:12:43,150 --> 00:12:46,034
- Ha Na!
- Ha Na!

211
00:13:08,304 --> 00:13:10,914
What the hell are the police doing?

212
00:13:10,914 --> 00:13:14,424
Put him under surveillance.
Form a task force. Do something!

213
00:13:14,424 --> 00:13:19,909
How have they failed to stop
or catch that rat for years?

214
00:13:19,909 --> 00:13:21,242
Screw procedure.

215
00:13:21,242 --> 00:13:23,759
I want an update on the investigation by...

216
00:13:23,759 --> 00:13:26,038
[Six Months Earlier]

217
00:13:27,406 --> 00:13:29,946
<i>- Emotional numbness?
- Yes.</i>

218
00:13:29,946 --> 00:13:36,546
<i>Your brain is slower to register
what you're feeling, even joy or sadness.</i>

219
00:13:36,546 --> 00:13:37,898
<i>Why me...</i>

220
00:13:37,898 --> 00:13:42,904
<i>It can happen to people like you,
who constantly manage their emotions.</i>

221
00:13:42,904 --> 00:13:45,503
<i>The mind can get overloaded too.</i>

222
00:13:45,503 --> 00:13:48,494
<i>But it shouldn't affect
your day-to-day life much.</i>

223
00:13:48,494 --> 00:13:53,155
<i>Could it affect my acting?</i>

224
00:13:53,155 --> 00:13:54,645
<i>It's possible.</i>

225
00:13:54,645 --> 00:13:57,733
<i>It impairs your ability
to feel and express emotions.</i>

226
00:14:01,235 --> 00:14:03,688
Get that in writing.

227
00:14:05,947 --> 00:14:08,315
Hello, Reporter Kim?

228
00:14:10,354 --> 00:14:12,927
I think it was around here.

229
00:14:17,972 --> 00:14:19,673
This guy.

230
00:14:23,010 --> 00:14:25,743
Can you zoom in from a better angle?

231
00:14:27,076 --> 00:14:29,419
The image is too pixelated...

232
00:14:30,623 --> 00:14:33,614
Is that a scar?

233
00:14:33,614 --> 00:14:35,115
Hard to tell.

234
00:16:32,006 --> 00:16:34,456
Why'd you turn the lights off?

235
00:16:34,456 --> 00:16:36,716
I need to take my makeup off.

236
00:16:36,716 --> 00:16:38,266
Then get up.

237
00:16:38,266 --> 00:16:40,314
I have no energy.

238
00:16:40,314 --> 00:16:43,640
I can't even lift a finger.

239
00:16:45,373 --> 00:16:47,884
I'm not washing your face for you.

240
00:16:49,532 --> 00:16:53,987
You think just anyone gets to touch my face?

241
00:16:54,983 --> 00:16:56,753
We're leaving at 11 tomorrow, right?

242
00:16:56,753 --> 00:16:58,283
Wash up and get some sleep.

243
00:16:58,283 --> 00:16:59,828
I'm leaving.

244
00:17:00,559 --> 00:17:02,619
Take my makeup off for me.

245
00:17:05,399 --> 00:17:07,289
Just for tonight.

246
00:17:07,289 --> 00:17:10,069
I have a dress fitting tomorrow.

247
00:17:11,448 --> 00:17:14,198
Just this once.

248
00:17:14,198 --> 00:17:15,652
Please?

249
00:18:15,592 --> 00:18:17,108
Oh, right.

250
00:18:17,108 --> 00:18:20,673
That camcorder's still
in the living room cabinet.

251
00:18:20,673 --> 00:18:22,396
Oh, yeah.

252
00:18:22,396 --> 00:18:24,656
It doesn't even turn on anymore.

253
00:18:26,289 --> 00:18:27,526
You should've had it fixed.

254
00:18:27,526 --> 00:18:29,716
It was already junk when I bought it.

255
00:18:29,716 --> 00:18:31,913
It's probably beyond repair.

256
00:18:36,065 --> 00:18:38,077
Don't you ever get tired of it?

257
00:18:39,145 --> 00:18:40,217
Of what?

258
00:18:40,217 --> 00:18:42,718
Being around me.

259
00:18:42,718 --> 00:18:44,306
Being my friend.

260
00:18:47,013 --> 00:18:50,606
You don't exactly give me time to get bored.

261
00:18:50,606 --> 00:18:53,110
True. You've got a point.

262
00:18:53,110 --> 00:18:55,779
I am pretty irresistible.

263
00:18:57,815 --> 00:18:59,491
Did you take your meds?

264
00:19:01,709 --> 00:19:03,041
Yeah.

265
00:19:03,041 --> 00:19:05,240
Getting sleepy?

266
00:19:05,240 --> 00:19:07,153
I think so.

267
00:19:08,660 --> 00:19:10,744
Want me to put a face mask on you?

268
00:19:10,744 --> 00:19:12,262
Yeah.

269
00:19:23,671 --> 00:19:26,829
[No Caller ID]

270
00:19:45,434 --> 00:19:46,897
- You were amazing!</i>

271
00:19:46,921 --> 00:19:48,386
<i>Let's meet up soon.</i>

272
00:19:49,534 --> 00:19:51,405
<i>You landed, right?</i>

273
00:19:53,696 --> 00:19:56,255
[My Boss]

274
00:19:56,979 --> 00:19:58,814
Yeah, I just landed.

275
00:19:58,814 --> 00:19:59,852
Where are you?

276
00:19:59,852 --> 00:20:03,402
<i>Where else? In your heart, of course.</i>

277
00:20:03,402 --> 00:20:05,154
Not Jung Woo Jae's?

278
00:20:05,154 --> 00:20:08,228
<i>Why? What are you sulking about now?</i>

279
00:20:08,228 --> 00:20:11,510
You said you love him more than anyone.

280
00:20:11,510 --> 00:20:12,912
News to me.

281
00:20:12,912 --> 00:20:14,875
<i>Oh, babe.</i>

282
00:20:14,875 --> 00:20:17,485
<i>You seriously didn't know?</i>

283
00:20:18,292 --> 00:20:19,119
What?

284
00:20:19,119 --> 00:20:23,987
Of course I love Jung Woo Jae.
More than life itself.

285
00:20:24,683 --> 00:20:25,716
Then what about me?

286
00:20:25,716 --> 00:20:27,952
You're...

287
00:20:29,876 --> 00:20:34,308
You're my boss for life.

288
00:20:34,308 --> 00:20:36,308
- What?
<i>- You're the boss, so...</i>

289
00:20:36,308 --> 00:20:38,802
you're stuck leading me till I die.

290
00:20:38,802 --> 00:20:40,481
Seo Ye Rang.

291
00:20:40,481 --> 00:20:42,205
Lucky you.

292
00:20:42,205 --> 00:20:44,007
You're thrilled, right?

293
00:20:45,876 --> 00:20:50,305
Sorry, I'm really not
in the mood to be thrilled.

294
00:20:50,305 --> 00:20:52,125
Why? Something happen?

295
00:20:52,125 --> 00:20:53,649
Well...

296
00:20:53,649 --> 00:20:55,705
It's about Ha Na's article.

297
00:20:55,705 --> 00:20:57,111
Yoon Ha Na?

298
00:20:57,111 --> 00:20:59,331
What about her?

299
00:20:59,331 --> 00:21:01,555
Come on, look.

300
00:21:01,555 --> 00:21:03,398
How do I look? Normal?

301
00:21:03,398 --> 00:21:05,658
Like none of this got to me?

302
00:21:07,734 --> 00:21:09,341
How about this face?

303
00:21:12,271 --> 00:21:15,223
That's your press conference face.

304
00:21:18,811 --> 00:21:20,597
Smile again.

305
00:21:28,505 --> 00:21:30,167
Got it. Toothpaste commercial?

306
00:21:30,167 --> 00:21:31,949
Stop messing around.

307
00:21:31,949 --> 00:21:35,063
Oh, that one. That looked the most natural.

308
00:21:35,063 --> 00:21:37,359
I'm not asking you anymore.

309
00:21:42,553 --> 00:21:44,837
Just pretend they're all me.

310
00:21:44,837 --> 00:21:46,823
Everyone out there.

311
00:21:47,921 --> 00:21:51,174
Just relax, like you are now.

312
00:21:54,561 --> 00:21:56,260
[Ha Na Smiles Brightly with Eyeless Doll]

313
00:21:59,228 --> 00:22:01,021
Hello.

314
00:22:01,021 --> 00:22:03,189
- Hello.
- Hello.

315
00:22:03,189 --> 00:22:04,201
Oh my!

316
00:22:04,201 --> 00:22:06,263
My sweetheart! You're here!

317
00:22:06,263 --> 00:22:08,413
- How have you been?
- Oh my.

318
00:22:08,413 --> 00:22:11,312
This is for you.
It's from the most famous patissier in Paris.

319
00:22:11,312 --> 00:22:14,784
- Oh my!
- The sugar work is so delicate...

320
00:22:14,784 --> 00:22:16,994
It reminded me of the beading on your dresses.

321
00:22:16,994 --> 00:22:18,093
My goodness!

322
00:22:18,093 --> 00:22:20,569
You didn't have to!

323
00:22:20,569 --> 00:22:22,397
I'm so touched.

324
00:22:22,397 --> 00:22:24,500
You're just too sweet. I adore you.

325
00:22:24,500 --> 00:22:25,461
Eun Jung, Ji Yoon.

326
00:22:25,461 --> 00:22:28,631
These are for you.
Have one when you need a sugar boost.

327
00:22:28,631 --> 00:22:30,675
Ji Yoon, you cut your bangs!

328
00:22:30,675 --> 00:22:32,551
They look so cute.

329
00:22:32,551 --> 00:22:34,637
You're always so thoughtful.

330
00:22:34,637 --> 00:22:36,185
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

331
00:22:36,185 --> 00:22:37,390
By the way...

332
00:22:37,390 --> 00:22:38,943
You saw the article, right?

333
00:22:39,884 --> 00:22:43,759
"Chucky and the Joker land
at Incheon Airport..."

334
00:22:43,759 --> 00:22:46,553
I need to look drop-dead gorgeous
at this awards show.

335
00:22:46,553 --> 00:22:49,110
No more Joker jokes.

336
00:22:49,110 --> 00:22:51,016
So what am I wearing?

337
00:22:51,016 --> 00:22:52,405
Leave it to me.

338
00:22:52,405 --> 00:22:53,519
Trust me.

339
00:22:53,519 --> 00:22:55,449
Come on, get in there.

340
00:22:55,449 --> 00:22:58,619
You look fabulous today!

341
00:22:58,619 --> 00:23:00,693
Welcome. Come on.

342
00:23:00,693 --> 00:23:02,957
I went with a G-Dragon look today.

343
00:23:02,957 --> 00:23:05,650
Ms. Yoon's fitting is done.

344
00:23:16,650 --> 00:23:20,820
Oh my god.

345
00:23:46,172 --> 00:23:48,252
Oh wow. Gorgeous.

346
00:23:48,252 --> 00:23:53,188
My dress looks even better on you.

347
00:23:55,902 --> 00:23:57,260
Hello.

348
00:23:57,260 --> 00:23:58,594
Hey, what are you doing here?

349
00:23:58,594 --> 00:23:59,597
Hi.

350
00:23:59,597 --> 00:24:02,850
- What was with that photo yesterday?
- Oh, you're here.

351
00:24:02,850 --> 00:24:04,904
I called him.

352
00:24:07,158 --> 00:24:08,494
Oh, yeah.

353
00:24:08,494 --> 00:24:11,567
Right. Big brother came to see you.

354
00:24:11,567 --> 00:24:13,069
You think I'm here to try on dresses?

355
00:24:13,069 --> 00:24:16,957
Big brother, my foot.
You're only two minutes older.

356
00:24:16,957 --> 00:24:19,325
Two minutes is a huge difference.

357
00:24:19,325 --> 00:24:22,203
Why has it been so long since you've come by?

358
00:24:22,203 --> 00:24:25,569
Didn't Ha Na tell you how much I missed you?

359
00:24:25,569 --> 00:24:27,875
- She didn't.
- My goodness!

360
00:24:27,875 --> 00:24:30,252
Oh, wow! Look at that body.

361
00:24:30,252 --> 00:24:33,172
A work of art.

362
00:24:33,172 --> 00:24:37,343
Let me make you a killer suit
to celebrate that gold medal.

363
00:24:37,343 --> 00:24:40,231
I'm good, but I appreciate it.

364
00:24:40,231 --> 00:24:41,305
Don't just appreciate it.

365
00:24:41,305 --> 00:24:43,881
Take the gifts!

366
00:24:44,602 --> 00:24:47,049
Don't smile at me like that!

367
00:24:47,049 --> 00:24:50,786
You're making my heart race.

368
00:24:50,786 --> 00:24:52,733
So...

369
00:24:52,733 --> 00:24:55,194
- Shall we go with this one?
- Yes, this is the one!

370
00:24:55,194 --> 00:24:56,362
It's perfect.

371
00:24:56,362 --> 00:24:58,808
Absolutely beautiful!

372
00:24:59,818 --> 00:25:01,901
I'm making you something. No arguments.

373
00:25:01,901 --> 00:25:03,701
Really, I'm fine.

374
00:25:05,330 --> 00:25:06,657
What?

375
00:25:06,657 --> 00:25:08,541
Emotional what?

376
00:25:08,541 --> 00:25:11,336
My emotions are on strike.

377
00:25:11,336 --> 00:25:12,709
Is that an actual diagnosis?

378
00:25:12,709 --> 00:25:15,006
That's private medical information.

379
00:25:15,006 --> 00:25:17,217
You don't need the details.

380
00:25:17,217 --> 00:25:18,582
Just tell me what's going on.

381
00:25:18,582 --> 00:25:20,595
I did. That's exactly what it is.

382
00:25:20,595 --> 00:25:24,549
Funny things aren't funny,
and sad things don't make me sad.

383
00:25:24,549 --> 00:25:28,181
My emotions won't do their job,
so they're on strike.

384
00:25:29,970 --> 00:25:34,502
Babe, am I the only one confused?
What is she even saying?

385
00:25:34,502 --> 00:25:37,035
Just eat this.

386
00:25:40,906 --> 00:25:42,242
- Spicy, but good.
- Right?

387
00:25:42,242 --> 00:25:43,755
Yeah.

388
00:25:44,570 --> 00:25:46,162
So...

389
00:25:46,162 --> 00:25:50,000
she's saying she can't really
feel emotions right now?

390
00:25:50,000 --> 00:25:51,105
Yeah.

391
00:25:51,105 --> 00:25:54,462
For real? Even that nasty temper of hers?

392
00:25:54,462 --> 00:25:55,791
Enough.

393
00:25:55,791 --> 00:25:57,666
Yoon Ha Ru, stop.

394
00:26:02,026 --> 00:26:05,724
Watching you play sweet
for the cameras makes me gag.

395
00:26:05,724 --> 00:26:08,763
You had a runny nose till second grade,
and now you act like a goddess.

396
00:26:08,763 --> 00:26:13,308
You're two minutes younger
and somehow look older than me.

397
00:26:18,090 --> 00:26:20,155
Crispy and good.

398
00:26:20,155 --> 00:26:21,490
Oh my.

399
00:26:22,602 --> 00:26:23,856
Don't bother.

400
00:26:23,856 --> 00:26:27,833
I don't have a shred of emotion
or energy to waste on you.

401
00:26:27,833 --> 00:26:30,775
- No way...
- I need to sleep. I'm filming tomorrow.

402
00:26:30,775 --> 00:26:33,828
- Oh my dear, what happened...
- Don't be dramatic.

403
00:26:33,828 --> 00:26:35,885
Once I'm better,
you're the first one I'm killing.

404
00:26:35,885 --> 00:26:40,276
My emotions stopped working, not my brain.

405
00:26:47,364 --> 00:26:48,975
- David.
- "David?"

406
00:26:48,975 --> 00:26:51,895
This is the biggest surprise ever.

407
00:26:51,895 --> 00:26:54,064
- Can we talk in private?
- What? A guy?

408
00:26:54,064 --> 00:26:57,490
He directed "Lunard Crystal," you idiot.

409
00:27:00,362 --> 00:27:04,366
Your favorite director
that no one's ever heard of?

410
00:27:04,366 --> 00:27:06,910
He won the Grand Jury Prize
at Sundance this year.

411
00:27:06,910 --> 00:27:09,920
He's Hollywood's hottest
new director right now.

412
00:27:09,920 --> 00:27:11,081
Okay.

413
00:27:11,081 --> 00:27:14,372
- Hollywood?
- Oh my God.

414
00:27:14,372 --> 00:27:17,216
You really mean Ha Na?

415
00:27:17,216 --> 00:27:18,806
It's a casting offer.

416
00:27:18,806 --> 00:27:20,768
A casting offer!

417
00:27:21,737 --> 00:27:23,892
Absolutely.

418
00:27:23,892 --> 00:27:25,581
David.

419
00:27:25,581 --> 00:27:29,808
She read the script
and she was like, genuinely impressed.

420
00:27:29,808 --> 00:27:32,040
I'm tired. I'm going to bed.

421
00:27:33,925 --> 00:27:35,450
What?

422
00:27:35,450 --> 00:27:38,905
Her favorite director offered her a role,
and she didn't even brag?

423
00:27:38,905 --> 00:27:40,704
She didn't even jump for joy...

424
00:27:40,704 --> 00:27:42,480
Is this real life?

425
00:27:42,480 --> 00:27:44,343
- Open up.
- Okay.

426
00:27:51,778 --> 00:27:54,202
- Sorry, I have to leave early.
- It's okay.

427
00:27:54,202 --> 00:27:55,907
- Take good care of Ha Na.
- I will.

428
00:27:55,907 --> 00:27:57,703
- I'll call you.
- Okay.

429
00:27:57,703 --> 00:27:59,674
Love you.

430
00:27:59,674 --> 00:28:00,653
- I'm off.
- Okay.

431
00:28:00,653 --> 00:28:02,527
- See you.
- Yeah.

432
00:28:02,527 --> 00:28:03,606
- Get home safe.
- I will.

433
00:28:03,606 --> 00:28:04,972
Bye.

434
00:28:08,891 --> 00:28:11,830
Hey, how long has Ha Na been like this?

435
00:28:11,830 --> 00:28:15,139
Hey. I'm her paid bodyguard.

436
00:28:15,139 --> 00:28:16,873
I can't tell you anything.

437
00:28:16,873 --> 00:28:17,934
You little...

438
00:28:17,934 --> 00:28:19,700
Seriously...

439
00:28:20,460 --> 00:28:22,336
Hey.

440
00:28:22,336 --> 00:28:24,607
Remember?

441
00:28:24,607 --> 00:28:26,538
Back in 11th grade,

442
00:28:26,538 --> 00:28:30,154
the one time I beat you.

443
00:28:30,154 --> 00:28:33,825
<i>I finally beat you.</i>

444
00:28:33,825 --> 00:28:35,502
<i>What?</i>

445
00:28:35,502 --> 00:28:37,620
<i>You lost. What's so funny?</i>

446
00:28:37,620 --> 00:28:39,747
<i>- You're so annoying.
- That's the point.</i>

447
00:28:39,747 --> 00:28:42,026
<i>Why do I feel like I lost?</i>

448
00:28:42,026 --> 00:28:44,085
<i>No. You totally beat me today.</i>

449
00:28:44,085 --> 00:28:46,004
<i>Congrats, Yoon Ha Ru.</i>

450
00:28:46,004 --> 00:28:48,511
<i>- Okay.
- Smile.</i>

451
00:28:48,511 --> 00:28:51,935
<i>One, two, three.</i>

452
00:28:51,935 --> 00:28:54,503
<i>Wait! Let me in!</i>

453
00:28:54,503 --> 00:28:56,973
<i>- Okay, smile.
- Wait!</i>

454
00:28:56,973 --> 00:28:58,876
<i>Hey, come here.</i>

455
00:28:58,876 --> 00:29:00,712
<i>What?</i>

456
00:29:00,712 --> 00:29:02,604
<i>Switch places with me.</i>

457
00:29:02,604 --> 00:29:04,593
<i>Why?</i>

458
00:29:04,593 --> 00:29:06,897
<i>Just shut up and switch.</i>

459
00:29:07,587 --> 00:29:09,110
<i>Oppa.</i>

460
00:29:09,110 --> 00:29:10,471
<i>What? "Oppa?"</i>

461
00:29:10,471 --> 00:29:12,177
<i>Fine, fine.</i>

462
00:29:15,731 --> 00:29:18,908
<i>- Ha Ru, squeeze in.
- Okay.</i>

463
00:29:21,982 --> 00:29:25,766
<i>One, two, three!</i>

464
00:29:33,314 --> 00:29:36,087
Of course I remember.

465
00:29:36,087 --> 00:29:42,053
Do you know what Ha Na
whispered in my ear that day?

466
00:29:43,991 --> 00:29:46,440
What did she say?

467
00:29:46,440 --> 00:29:48,071
Curious?

468
00:29:48,071 --> 00:29:49,447
Yeah.

469
00:29:49,447 --> 00:29:50,867
Come here.

470
00:29:52,395 --> 00:29:53,890
Closer.

471
00:29:56,267 --> 00:29:59,160
It's a secret.

472
00:29:59,160 --> 00:30:00,536
Oh, come on!

473
00:30:00,536 --> 00:30:02,081
I'm not telling you either.

474
00:30:02,081 --> 00:30:06,591
You tell me first if you want to know.

475
00:30:13,821 --> 00:30:15,870
Just...

476
00:30:15,870 --> 00:30:18,843
Don't do this anymore.

477
00:31:23,326 --> 00:31:24,935
[Anonymous Forum]

478
00:31:26,932 --> 00:31:28,629
[The Truth About Yoon Ha Na
Who Fooled the Nation]

479
00:31:29,620 --> 00:31:31,938
I don't want to go.

480
00:31:31,938 --> 00:31:33,354
You want me to leave?

481
00:31:33,354 --> 00:31:35,032
Sun Ah.

482
00:31:35,032 --> 00:31:36,844
Do you really want me to go?

483
00:31:38,129 --> 00:31:39,886
Why won't you stop me?

484
00:31:39,886 --> 00:31:43,720
Why... won't you ever let me in?

485
00:32:00,258 --> 00:32:01,839
That's it.

486
00:32:07,789 --> 00:32:09,225
Cry.

487
00:32:10,683 --> 00:32:12,313
Come on, cry.

488
00:32:13,803 --> 00:32:15,358
Please...

489
00:32:30,031 --> 00:32:30,908
Cut.

490
00:32:30,908 --> 00:32:32,561
Cut!

491
00:32:34,819 --> 00:32:36,232
Sorry, sir.

492
00:32:36,232 --> 00:32:39,486
Maybe I'm dehydrated. Why won't the tears come?

493
00:32:39,486 --> 00:32:42,120
Crying's my specialty.
This shouldn't be happening.

494
00:32:42,120 --> 00:32:43,145
Right?

495
00:32:43,145 --> 00:32:45,385
It's okay. We'll go again.

496
00:32:45,385 --> 00:32:46,833
Let's take a quick break.

497
00:32:46,833 --> 00:32:48,638
- Let's reconvene in ten.
- We'll take ten.

498
00:32:48,638 --> 00:32:51,215
- Okay!
- Ten-minute break!

499
00:32:52,041 --> 00:32:53,504
Is something wrong?

500
00:32:53,504 --> 00:32:56,715
No. I told you. I'm just dehydrated.

501
00:32:56,715 --> 00:32:58,290
If today is too much, tell me.

502
00:32:58,290 --> 00:33:00,967
We can move things around. Whatever you need.

503
00:33:00,967 --> 00:33:02,897
I'm your upperclassman, remember?

504
00:33:02,897 --> 00:33:04,630
Put me to use.

505
00:33:04,630 --> 00:33:06,590
Okay. I will.

506
00:33:06,590 --> 00:33:07,640
Thanks.

507
00:33:07,640 --> 00:33:09,482
Don't worry. Get some rest.

508
00:33:45,467 --> 00:33:48,028
This is so frustrating.

509
00:33:48,028 --> 00:33:50,914
Why can't I cry?

510
00:33:51,601 --> 00:33:54,397
Why is it so hard?

511
00:33:57,259 --> 00:33:59,402
Just drink this first.

512
00:34:07,229 --> 00:34:09,245
It's good.

513
00:34:17,466 --> 00:34:19,455
What do you think it is?

514
00:34:20,945 --> 00:34:22,879
What?

515
00:34:22,879 --> 00:34:25,359
What Sun Ah's feeling.

516
00:34:31,505 --> 00:34:33,132
Regret.

517
00:34:35,118 --> 00:34:36,401
"Regret?"

518
00:34:37,405 --> 00:34:38,868
Yeah.

519
00:34:42,552 --> 00:34:44,929
She doesn't believe in herself.

520
00:34:44,929 --> 00:34:47,899
Jae Hee shines so bright,

521
00:34:47,899 --> 00:34:50,732
she thinks she's not good enough for him.

522
00:34:51,699 --> 00:34:56,610
She loves him so much, but she can't show it.

523
00:34:58,088 --> 00:35:00,628
Jae Hee kept giving her chances.

524
00:35:00,628 --> 00:35:02,628
To come closer.

525
00:35:03,458 --> 00:35:05,328
To hold him.

526
00:35:08,370 --> 00:35:10,074
But still...

527
00:35:10,805 --> 00:35:13,478
Sun Ah let every chance slip away.

528
00:35:15,393 --> 00:35:17,934
She never told him how she felt.

529
00:35:19,564 --> 00:35:24,199
And now she'll never see him again.

530
00:35:24,199 --> 00:35:26,342
She wishes she'd said something...

531
00:35:28,514 --> 00:35:30,514
She regrets it so much.

532
00:35:35,790 --> 00:35:39,313
That's how I think Sun Ah feels.

533
00:35:43,838 --> 00:35:45,938
That's sad.

534
00:35:49,169 --> 00:35:51,006
Ha Na.

535
00:35:51,006 --> 00:35:52,279
You need to go back in.

536
00:35:52,279 --> 00:35:54,669
Let's get your makeup touched up.

537
00:36:05,093 --> 00:36:06,758
Sir.

538
00:36:06,758 --> 00:36:09,726
- Have some coffee.
- Thanks.

539
00:36:11,460 --> 00:36:14,304
What's gotten into Ha Na lately?

540
00:36:14,304 --> 00:36:18,663
It's not just the crying.
There's no emotion in her acting at all.

541
00:36:18,663 --> 00:36:20,400
And she's going to Hollywood like that?

542
00:36:20,400 --> 00:36:22,220
No way.

543
00:36:23,130 --> 00:36:25,840
She's not doing your next project anyway, huh?

544
00:36:25,840 --> 00:36:27,740
That's probably a good thing for us.

545
00:36:27,740 --> 00:36:30,561
How did she fall off so fast?

546
00:36:30,561 --> 00:36:33,416
She might just embarrass herself
in Hollywood...

547
00:36:33,416 --> 00:36:35,181
Seriously...

548
00:36:35,181 --> 00:36:36,775
Hey.

549
00:36:37,504 --> 00:36:38,949
Yes?

550
00:36:38,949 --> 00:36:40,928
Watch what you say.

551
00:36:40,928 --> 00:36:42,445
She's one of our actors.

552
00:36:42,445 --> 00:36:44,312
- Sorry.
- Yeah.

553
00:36:44,312 --> 00:36:45,828
Sir!

554
00:36:46,524 --> 00:36:48,009
This...

555
00:36:48,684 --> 00:36:51,209
- What is it?
- You need to see this.

556
00:36:51,209 --> 00:36:52,665
[Yoon Ha Na Under Fire Over Attitude
and Drug Addiction Allegations]

557
00:36:55,126 --> 00:36:57,110
<i>For what? I already can't stand him.</i>

558
00:36:57,110 --> 00:36:58,579
[Taking pills!]

559
00:36:58,579 --> 00:37:01,374
<i>You know who I am, right?</i>

560
00:37:01,374 --> 00:37:03,113
<i>I'm Yoon Ha Na.</i>

561
00:37:06,197 --> 00:37:07,674
CEO Seo is here.

562
00:37:07,674 --> 00:37:10,174
- Oh, ma'am.
- Ye Rang? When did you get here?

563
00:37:10,174 --> 00:37:12,265
- Get the car ready. Now.
- Sorry?

564
00:37:12,265 --> 00:37:14,429
What are you talking about?
We're still shooting.

565
00:37:14,429 --> 00:37:16,804
- Hurry!
- Yes.

566
00:37:17,636 --> 00:37:19,885
What's going on?

567
00:37:19,885 --> 00:37:21,885
Damn it.

568
00:37:35,493 --> 00:37:37,032
Ha Na.

569
00:37:39,881 --> 00:37:41,165
Stop drinking.

570
00:37:41,165 --> 00:37:44,037
- Let go.
- I said stop!

571
00:37:50,650 --> 00:37:52,132
Take a break.

572
00:37:52,132 --> 00:37:53,884
Ha Na.

573
00:37:53,884 --> 00:37:57,998
Since it's come to this,
take some time off and get treatment.

574
00:37:58,731 --> 00:38:03,282
You want me to make
those damn rumors look true?

575
00:38:03,282 --> 00:38:06,064
You just look like
you're having a really hard time.

576
00:38:08,200 --> 00:38:10,558
I'm perfectly fine.

577
00:38:13,573 --> 00:38:15,271
Ha Na.

578
00:38:16,146 --> 00:38:18,154
You're not fine.

579
00:38:18,787 --> 00:38:22,106
It's okay to let go when you need to.

580
00:38:23,151 --> 00:38:25,016
Like you did?

581
00:38:29,566 --> 00:38:30,696
What?

582
00:38:30,696 --> 00:38:35,593
You mean like when you gave up judo?

583
00:38:37,577 --> 00:38:40,753
- No, I...
- Taking a break?

584
00:38:40,753 --> 00:38:42,318
Sure, sounds great.

585
00:38:42,318 --> 00:38:45,721
But what do you get after running away?

586
00:38:45,721 --> 00:38:47,965
You ended up a bodyguard.

587
00:38:47,965 --> 00:38:49,989
I can't do that.

588
00:38:49,989 --> 00:38:52,002
I'm going to keep acting.

589
00:38:53,396 --> 00:38:55,157
I'm not taking a break.

590
00:39:58,064 --> 00:40:00,224
[Capturing Your Shining Moments]

591
00:40:22,410 --> 00:40:24,016
<i>Ta-da!</i>

592
00:40:24,016 --> 00:40:26,040
<i>Pretty, right?</i>

593
00:40:26,040 --> 00:40:27,452
<i>Yeah.</i>

594
00:40:28,666 --> 00:40:31,425
<i>Come on. It's not the end of the world.</i>

595
00:40:31,425 --> 00:40:34,904
<i>You can't do judo anymore.
So what? Is your life over?</i>

596
00:40:37,808 --> 00:40:39,607
<i>Look at me.</i>

597
00:40:41,930 --> 00:40:46,267
<i>To me, you're still just as amazing.</i>

598
00:40:46,267 --> 00:40:50,066
<i>Judo or no judo, nothing's changed.</i>

599
00:40:53,456 --> 00:40:56,945
<i>I'm not good at anything anymore.</i>

600
00:40:56,945 --> 00:40:59,450
<i>Sure you are.</i>

601
00:41:02,951 --> 00:41:05,151
<i>Protect me.</i>

602
00:41:05,151 --> 00:41:09,082
<i>When I become a famous actress someday,</i>

603
00:41:09,082 --> 00:41:11,033
<i>you can protect me.</i>

604
00:41:12,102 --> 00:41:14,832
<i>You are one of the best
high school judo players in the country.</i>

605
00:41:14,832 --> 00:41:17,096
<i>Who else could protect me?</i>

606
00:41:17,096 --> 00:41:18,642
<i>Right?</i>

607
00:41:18,642 --> 00:41:19,772
<i>Right?</i>

608
00:41:19,772 --> 00:41:21,662
<i>Right?</i>

609
00:41:21,662 --> 00:41:22,959
<i>Right?</i>

610
00:41:22,959 --> 00:41:24,166
<i>Right?</i>

611
00:41:24,166 --> 00:41:27,141
<i>- You smiled! Finally!
- I did not.</i>

612
00:41:27,141 --> 00:41:29,547
<i>You did.</i>

613
00:41:48,621 --> 00:41:50,599
Yoon Ha Na.

614
00:41:52,272 --> 00:41:54,586
You're the worst.

615
00:42:01,794 --> 00:42:03,711
Of course she's attending the awards.

616
00:42:03,711 --> 00:42:05,898
Just think about it.

617
00:42:05,898 --> 00:42:10,297
Do you really think she would act like that
on a plane full of people?

618
00:42:11,909 --> 00:42:14,206
Of course we have evidence to prove otherwise.

619
00:42:14,206 --> 00:42:19,261
If you still choose to believe
such ridiculous rumors, we're done here.

620
00:42:21,193 --> 00:42:22,943
Damn it!

621
00:42:22,943 --> 00:42:26,418
All this over some ridiculous rumor...

622
00:43:32,517 --> 00:43:34,059
Don't be scared.

623
00:43:34,059 --> 00:43:36,002
Just be yourself.

624
00:43:44,424 --> 00:43:46,419
So beautiful!

625
00:44:52,230 --> 00:44:54,932
When they laughed, we laughed with them.

626
00:44:54,932 --> 00:44:58,559
And when they cried,
they moved an entire nation.

627
00:44:58,559 --> 00:45:02,898
Now it's time to honor
the very best in Korean cinema.

628
00:45:02,898 --> 00:45:05,379
Best Actress.

629
00:45:05,379 --> 00:45:09,572
Presenting the award is last year's winner,
actress Lee Hyun Jin.

630
00:45:09,572 --> 00:45:14,226
Last year, Lee Hyun Jin starred in
"Silver Grass" as Hannah,

631
00:45:14,226 --> 00:45:19,787
a woman born and raised in America
who never truly found a place to belong,

632
00:45:19,787 --> 00:45:23,103
capturing an immigrant's loss and longing.

633
00:45:23,124 --> 00:45:28,938
Today, she is an acclaimed actress
whose work transcends borders and languages.

634
00:45:28,938 --> 00:45:30,557
Just leave it there, please.

635
00:45:30,557 --> 00:45:31,650
- Here?
- Thank you.

636
00:45:31,650 --> 00:45:33,340
- Have a good one.
- Thanks.

637
00:45:33,340 --> 00:45:35,140
I'll put these flowers inside.

638
00:45:35,911 --> 00:45:38,400
You can leave them here.
We'll deliver them all together.

639
00:45:38,400 --> 00:45:39,534
Okay.

640
00:45:39,534 --> 00:45:41,498
- These too...
- Just put them down there.

641
00:45:41,498 --> 00:45:42,918
Okay.

642
00:45:47,327 --> 00:45:50,142
Hello, I'm Lee Hyun Jin.

643
00:45:53,417 --> 00:45:55,345
Thank you.

644
00:45:55,345 --> 00:46:01,100
It feels like yesterday
I stood here with my heart pounding.

645
00:46:01,100 --> 00:46:04,763
I can't believe it's already been a year.

646
00:46:04,763 --> 00:46:08,006
<i>It feels strange being back up here.</i>

647
00:46:08,006 --> 00:46:12,195
<i>I can only imagine
how hard you worked behind the scenes,</i>

648
00:46:12,195 --> 00:46:16,056
through all those long, grueling days.

649
00:46:16,056 --> 00:46:17,898
For all the time and passion you poured

650
00:46:17,898 --> 00:46:19,994
- Ha Na.
- into your films...

651
00:46:19,994 --> 00:46:24,040
Whatever anyone says,
you're the best actress in the world to me.

652
00:46:24,040 --> 00:46:25,860
You know that, right?

653
00:46:25,860 --> 00:46:27,596
Of course I do.

654
00:46:27,596 --> 00:46:29,462
Thank you so much.

655
00:46:29,462 --> 00:46:32,093
Now, shall we see who won?

656
00:46:37,348 --> 00:46:41,781
The 30th Baekryong Film Awards, 2026.

657
00:46:41,781 --> 00:46:44,492
And the award for Best Actress goes to...

658
00:46:49,919 --> 00:46:53,778
Yoon Ha Na, from "I Was There in Your Night."

659
00:46:53,778 --> 00:46:55,598
Congratulations.

660
00:46:56,823 --> 00:46:59,993
In director Yang Jun Mo's film
"I Was There in Your Night,"

661
00:46:59,993 --> 00:47:02,268
Yoon Ha Na played Cha Hee,

662
00:47:02,268 --> 00:47:05,835
<i>capturing the finest shades of human emotion</i>

663
00:47:05,835 --> 00:47:09,106
in a performance that deeply moved audiences.

664
00:47:09,106 --> 00:47:15,091
Tonight feels like a fitting tribute
to all her dedication and sincerity.

665
00:47:15,091 --> 00:47:20,558
Now, let's hear from
this year's Best Actress, Yoon Ha Na.

666
00:47:22,928 --> 00:47:24,928
Thank you.

667
00:47:26,063 --> 00:47:29,818
This trophy feels especially heavy tonight.

668
00:47:45,624 --> 00:47:50,857
There's been a lot of talk about me lately.

669
00:47:52,548 --> 00:47:54,548
Those videos...

670
00:47:56,001 --> 00:47:57,261
They're real.

671
00:47:57,261 --> 00:48:01,574
I haven't exactly been myself lately.

672
00:48:02,600 --> 00:48:08,046
I've been having some trouble feeling emotions.

673
00:48:08,046 --> 00:48:10,941
So yes, I've been seeing a doctor.

674
00:48:10,941 --> 00:48:13,934
I'm taking medication and getting treatment.

675
00:48:13,934 --> 00:48:18,590
And yes, that was me
in the video from the plane.

676
00:48:18,590 --> 00:48:21,653
What's going on?

677
00:48:21,653 --> 00:48:23,203
Oh, dear...

678
00:48:23,203 --> 00:48:25,562
My poor girl...

679
00:48:25,562 --> 00:48:27,124
<i>But...</i>

680
00:48:27,124 --> 00:48:31,504
<i>Even if I'm a little broken,
I still know right from wrong.</i>

681
00:48:31,504 --> 00:48:37,700
The only person I've ever told
I can't stand is Yoon Ha Ru.

682
00:48:39,562 --> 00:48:42,807
If I ever said that to someone else
like in that edited clip,

683
00:48:42,807 --> 00:48:47,231
my mom would probably kill me first.

684
00:48:53,390 --> 00:48:57,738
I hope you'll believe me.

685
00:48:57,738 --> 00:48:59,538
And...

686
00:49:01,992 --> 00:49:06,923
I'm going to take
a little time off and come back.

687
00:49:07,619 --> 00:49:09,583
I won't be gone long.

688
00:49:09,583 --> 00:49:12,886
I bounce back pretty fast.

689
00:49:17,591 --> 00:49:19,542
<i>Thank you so much.</i>

690
00:49:26,264 --> 00:49:28,020
My daughter...

691
00:49:28,020 --> 00:49:29,736
You're the bomb.

692
00:49:29,736 --> 00:49:32,398
Two thumbs way up.

693
00:49:32,398 --> 00:49:35,878
Yeah... that was awesome.

694
00:49:38,609 --> 00:49:42,575
Would you stop stuffing your face
at a time like this?

695
00:49:43,503 --> 00:49:46,006
Leave him alone.

696
00:49:46,006 --> 00:49:48,945
- I loved your movie.
- Let's get a picture. One, two!

697
00:49:48,945 --> 00:49:51,547
One more. One, two!

698
00:49:51,547 --> 00:49:52,704
Beautiful.

699
00:49:52,704 --> 00:49:54,109
- Congratulations.
- Thank you.

700
00:49:54,109 --> 00:49:55,213
Thank you.

701
00:49:55,213 --> 00:49:56,966
It's such an honor to get a photo with you.

702
00:49:56,966 --> 00:49:59,535
- Thank you.
- Get some rest.

703
00:50:00,413 --> 00:50:02,759
- Congratulations, Ha Na.
- Thank you.

704
00:50:02,759 --> 00:50:03,847
- We'll head over first.
- Okay.

705
00:50:03,847 --> 00:50:05,431
- You looked amazing tonight.
- See you.

706
00:50:05,431 --> 00:50:07,607
- I'll get the car ready.
- Okay.

707
00:50:07,607 --> 00:50:10,102
- Should we get going too?
- Yeah, let's go.

708
00:50:10,102 --> 00:50:12,986
We'll head over first. Take your time.

709
00:50:12,986 --> 00:50:15,897
Ha Na, you were incredible tonight.

710
00:50:15,897 --> 00:50:18,069
- See you later.
- Thanks.

711
00:50:18,069 --> 00:50:19,597
See you soon.

712
00:50:22,296 --> 00:50:23,657
Take care of Ha Na.

713
00:50:23,657 --> 00:50:26,770
- Let's get you changed.
- Yeah.

714
00:50:47,423 --> 00:50:49,650
Everyone's leaving. Let's go.

715
00:50:49,650 --> 00:50:51,119
Yeah.

716
00:50:54,105 --> 00:50:56,105
Hey, Jung Woo Jae.

717
00:50:58,526 --> 00:51:00,423
You know...

718
00:51:01,320 --> 00:51:03,856
about what I said yesterday...

719
00:51:04,732 --> 00:51:06,622
Oh, hold on.

720
00:51:06,622 --> 00:51:08,184
[Seok Min]

721
00:51:09,850 --> 00:51:12,164
<i>Ha Na, we're all ready.</i>

722
00:51:12,164 --> 00:51:14,477
Yeah, I'm coming out now.

723
00:51:15,918 --> 00:51:17,704
Woo Jae.

724
00:51:18,497 --> 00:51:20,756
I mean...

725
00:51:20,756 --> 00:51:23,022
about yesterday...

726
00:51:26,512 --> 00:51:29,338
Why the long face on a night like this?

727
00:51:30,030 --> 00:51:31,934
I'm fine.

728
00:51:31,934 --> 00:51:33,741
Don't worry about me.

729
00:51:37,357 --> 00:51:38,950
Let's go.

730
00:51:40,067 --> 00:51:41,507
Okay.

731
00:51:45,588 --> 00:51:46,823
[Actress Yoon Ha Na]

732
00:52:26,220 --> 00:52:27,323
Woo Jae.

733
00:52:27,347 --> 00:52:29,058
Woo Jae, open the door.

734
00:52:29,058 --> 00:52:30,729
Jung Woo Jae!

735
00:52:48,251 --> 00:52:50,692
Jung Woo Jae!

736
00:52:50,692 --> 00:52:52,036
Jung Woo Jae!

737
00:52:52,036 --> 00:52:54,005
What's wrong? Hey!

738
00:52:55,392 --> 00:52:57,418
Jung Woo Jae!

739
00:53:07,511 --> 00:53:09,337
What are you doing here?

740
00:53:14,835 --> 00:53:17,252
Mr. Jung! Mr. Jung!

741
00:53:26,773 --> 00:53:28,012
Woo Jae...

742
00:53:28,012 --> 00:53:29,811
Jung Woo Jae!

743
00:53:30,948 --> 00:53:32,822
Oh my...

744
00:53:32,822 --> 00:53:35,033
Call an ambulance... Please!

745
00:53:35,033 --> 00:53:36,370
Okay.

746
00:53:36,370 --> 00:53:38,217
- I'll get help.
- Woo Jae.

747
00:53:38,217 --> 00:53:39,696
Stay with me.

748
00:53:39,696 --> 00:53:42,405
- Woo Jae.
- Emergency services?

749
00:53:53,018 --> 00:53:54,656
Ha Na.

750
00:54:12,837 --> 00:54:14,837
Thank goodness...

751
00:54:16,618 --> 00:54:18,039
No.

752
00:54:18,039 --> 00:54:19,449
No.

753
00:54:19,449 --> 00:54:21,271
This can't be...

754
00:54:36,421 --> 00:54:38,046
Woo Jae...

755
00:54:39,381 --> 00:54:41,273
Woo Jae.

756
00:54:41,882 --> 00:54:43,353
No...

757
00:54:43,353 --> 00:54:44,996
This can't be...

758
00:54:44,996 --> 00:54:46,513
Woo Jae.

759
00:54:46,513 --> 00:54:47,886
What do I do...

760
00:54:47,886 --> 00:54:50,416
No, Woo Jae...

761
00:54:50,416 --> 00:54:53,708
No way...

762
00:54:53,708 --> 00:54:57,235
Woo Jae, wake up.

763
00:54:57,235 --> 00:54:59,735
What do I do...

764
00:54:59,735 --> 00:55:02,466
<i>Actress Yoon Ha Na's bodyguard has died.</i>

765
00:55:02,466 --> 00:55:07,493
<i>The suspect reportedly entered the scene
disguised as a flower deliveryman.</i>

766
00:55:07,493 --> 00:55:13,182
<i>Police confirmed that someone
had been stalking Ms. Yoon for some time.</i>

767
00:55:13,182 --> 00:55:18,409
<i>It remains unclear whether
the suspect is the same person.</i>

768
00:55:18,409 --> 00:55:22,803
<i>Police are investigating
the possible connection and circumstances.</i>

769
00:55:22,803 --> 00:55:26,351
<i>Ms. Yoon is reportedly in a state of shock</i>

770
00:55:26,351 --> 00:55:30,490
<i>and has suspended all public appearances.</i>

771
00:55:40,398 --> 00:55:41,616
[Yoon Ha Na]

772
00:55:44,967 --> 00:55:46,194
[When you're feeling anxious]
[Cut back on caffeine and alcohol]

773
00:55:46,194 --> 00:55:47,650
[Only one coffee a day]
[Don't overthink things]

774
00:55:50,527 --> 00:55:52,639
[Ha Na's Medications]
[Precautions]

775
00:55:59,959 --> 00:56:02,133
These are all notes for me.

776
00:56:18,610 --> 00:56:20,203
What's this doing here?

777
00:56:20,203 --> 00:56:21,278
[Yoon Ha Na]

778
00:56:34,823 --> 00:56:36,751
<i>Is this recording?</i>

779
00:56:40,256 --> 00:56:42,798
<i>Hey, Yoon Ha Na.</i>

780
00:56:42,798 --> 00:56:44,479
<i>It's me.</i>

781
00:56:46,878 --> 00:56:50,262
<i>First off, congrats on Best Actress.</i>

782
00:56:54,298 --> 00:56:56,927
<i>The awards are actually tomorrow,</i>

783
00:56:56,927 --> 00:57:01,310
<i>but honestly, I can't see anyone else winning.</i>

784
00:57:01,310 --> 00:57:03,625
<i>So I'm recording this early.</i>

785
00:57:04,646 --> 00:57:10,109
<i>By now, you're probably holding that trophy,
over the moon.</i>

786
00:57:11,822 --> 00:57:13,837
Jung Woo Jae...

787
00:57:13,837 --> 00:57:15,699
<i>I got this camcorder fixed.</i>

788
00:57:15,699 --> 00:57:17,328
<i>Pretty good, right?</i>

789
00:57:18,067 --> 00:57:24,299
All our old videos were still on here.

790
00:57:24,299 --> 00:57:27,299
We really shone back then.

791
00:57:32,423 --> 00:57:34,293
And...

792
00:57:36,045 --> 00:57:39,193
You're still shining just as bright.

793
00:57:40,527 --> 00:57:43,129
So don't worry.

794
00:57:48,572 --> 00:57:51,571
To me, no one shines brighter...

795
00:57:53,184 --> 00:57:55,228
than you.

796
00:57:55,228 --> 00:57:57,042
Yoon Ha Na.

797
00:58:02,902 --> 00:58:05,666
<i>This is kind of embarrassing to say...</i>

798
00:58:05,666 --> 00:58:07,592
Woo Jae...

799
00:58:09,166 --> 00:58:11,377
Jung Woo Jae...

800
00:58:11,377 --> 00:58:15,085
<i>Ha Na, congratulations. I really mean it.</i>

801
01:00:38,207 --> 01:00:40,892
Jung Woo Jae... I miss him.

802
01:00:44,479 --> 01:00:46,745
I miss him so much.

803
01:03:19,890 --> 01:03:21,597
[2010 Haesol City Superintendent's Cup
Judo Tournament]

804
01:03:21,597 --> 01:03:24,224
<i>What is this? Is it a dream?</i>

805
01:03:24,224 --> 01:03:26,688
<i>"2010?"</i>

806
01:03:29,744 --> 01:03:31,527
Everyone in the center, please.

807
01:03:31,527 --> 01:03:34,633
<i>What? Is he talking to me?</i>

808
01:03:34,633 --> 01:03:36,569
Player Yoon Ha Ru, what are you doing?

809
01:03:36,569 --> 01:03:39,049
Come on, onto the mat, please.

810
01:03:39,049 --> 01:03:41,324
<i>Why is he telling me that?</i>

811
01:03:41,324 --> 01:03:43,956
<i>What is this?</i>

812
01:03:48,419 --> 01:03:50,270
<i>Woo Jae?</i>

813
01:03:59,306 --> 01:04:01,293
<i>Jung Woo Jae?</i>

814
01:04:08,177 --> 01:04:10,128
<i>Thank goodness...</i>

815
01:04:19,962 --> 01:04:24,404
<i>To me, no one shines brighter... than you.</i>

816
01:04:24,404 --> 01:04:25,855
<i>Yoon Ha Na.</i>

817
01:04:26,623 --> 01:04:28,321
Woo Jae!

818
01:04:59,773 --> 01:05:00,946
[Epilogue coming up]

819
01:05:12,969 --> 01:05:15,427
[Dive Into You]

820
01:05:16,143 --> 01:05:17,946
<i>Maybe we're still dreaming?</i>

821
01:05:17,946 --> 01:05:20,103
<i>Do you remember anything else?</i>

822
01:05:20,103 --> 01:05:22,542
<i>Where do you think you're touching,
you bastard?</i>

823
01:05:22,542 --> 01:05:26,395
<i>You and I, together, with the camcorder,
fall into a body of water.</i>

824
01:05:26,395 --> 01:05:27,418
<i>Are you okay?</i>

825
01:05:27,418 --> 01:05:29,172
<i>This is crazy!</i>

826
01:05:29,172 --> 01:05:30,341
<i>She's acting...</i>

827
01:05:30,341 --> 01:05:31,334
<i>Totally crazy.</i>

828
01:05:31,334 --> 01:05:32,470
<i>Even weirder than usual.</i>

829
01:05:32,470 --> 01:05:34,233
<i>This is no ordinary training camp.</i>

830
01:05:35,868 --> 01:05:38,069
<i>That place is like the wilderness.</i>

831
01:05:38,069 --> 01:05:41,332
<i>Hide it, he'll dig deeper.
Say you're fine, he'll get suspicious.</i>

832
01:05:41,332 --> 01:05:42,874
<i>What if some small action...</i>

833
01:05:42,874 --> 01:05:46,670
<i>ends up irreversibly changing our past?</i>

834
01:05:46,670 --> 01:05:48,408
<i>What do we do?</i>

835
01:05:48,408 --> 01:05:50,403
<i>We can save him.</i>

836
01:05:52,472 --> 01:05:56,587
[Epilogue]

837
01:06:02,565 --> 01:06:05,958
I could only recover a few of the videos.

838
01:06:09,353 --> 01:06:10,488
It works.

839
01:06:10,488 --> 01:06:12,211
Thank you.

840
01:06:13,481 --> 01:06:15,420
How much do I owe you?

841
01:06:20,363 --> 01:06:23,575
Just give me a thousand won.

842
01:06:24,340 --> 01:06:25,431
Sorry?

843
01:06:25,431 --> 01:06:27,002
But...

844
01:06:27,002 --> 01:06:28,612
It's fine.

845
01:06:29,663 --> 01:06:31,489
Thank you so much.

846
01:06:33,803 --> 01:06:39,426
<i>♪ At my age, after all these years ♪</i>

847
01:06:39,426 --> 01:06:44,508
<i>♪ What sweetness could heartbreak hold? ♪</i>

848
01:06:45,128 --> 01:06:49,938
<i>♪ Still, there's an empty space ♪</i>

849
01:06:49,938 --> 01:06:54,790
<i>♪ Somewhere in my heart ♪</i>

850
01:06:54,790 --> 01:07:00,657
<i>♪ For all that I've lost ♪</i>
